+# HPO admission B, revision2: portability base and independent validity gate
+
+This revision remains prepared and unpromoted. It preserves the original
+protocol and its hashes as historical revision1. The factorial arms, strongest
+SINGLE controls, search space, seed137, startup3, eight trials including the
+anchor,900-second study allocation,600-second/two-thread/1536MiB workers,
+classification grouped42/43 and regression forward0/1/2 cuts are unchanged.
+Operational cost and outer ML quality remain separate. No model fit or API
+call was made to prepare this revision.
+
+The isolated source now includes the exact tracked Windows portability changes
+from `70700ac03c5e177ebd527918d01d7b424754c8f7` (native2c). The runner also retains
+the original opt-in admission flag. The only subsequent base change is
+`tools/run_checks.py` from `d2a329a00082cdf08ea30bbf49dc0be4baf3a126`: shallow
+temporary fixtures and cleanup telemetry, followed by the explicitly authorized
+native2e one-line move of the fixture parent to `ROOT.parent/'t'` (workspace
+`work/t`). The new tests remain registered. No runtime fix was added beyond2c.
+`hpo.py` after LF normalization is
+identical to the reviewed revision1 admission implementation. Existing modified
+files preserve canonical CRLF endings for a minimal patch; new files use LF. Compilation
+differs from native2c in only `automl_runner.py` and `automl_search_hpo.py`;
+the other66 flat files, including model adapters and requirements, match.
+These are source facts, not a claim of measured prediction or metric parity.
+
+The previous benchmark's `completed` lifecycle and exit0 could coexist with
+an outer timeout/error or a study clipped by the enclosing deadline. The
+benchmark now records initial requested/allocated study seconds and clipping,
+saved outer partition byte hashes, worker thread count, and final task/harness
+integrity. It explicitly labels lifecycle completion as insufficient for
+qualification. Worker JSON is read as UTF-8 and child UTF-8 configuration is
+explicit. These reporting changes do not choose a model or alter its objective.
+
+`tools/qualify_hpo.py` is a separate read-only, no-fit validity gate. Pass all
+policy/cut result files for one task and the revision2 JSON plan. It requires
+every predeclared cut and both policies/samplers, the unchanged strong control,
+matching frozen compiled source and harness files, verified task/input bytes,
+successful finite outer primary metrics, and nonnumeric failed inner values.
+It checks saved outer and inner NPZ indices, their hashes, inner containment,
+group-overlap declarations, and identical partitions across the four arms.
+It also checks the selected inner winner matches the outer refit recipe.
+An unchanged control with drifting outer metric invalidates its paired cut.
+
+Each study must have received the full900-second initial allocation. An early
+measured admission stop remains valid; external deadline clipping is not
+equal-budget evidence. Missing or repeated cuts, failed outer workers,
+nonfinite/boolean metrics, altered source/inputs/controls or leaking inner
+rows fail qualification. A valid negative-quality screen remains evidence.
+The tool reports per-cut differences and per-task outer means, including
+equal-budget TPE-versus-random differences and successful guided counts.
+It never substitutes zero for a failed metric.
+
+This gate validates saved artifacts and protocol metadata. It does not
+recompute outer metrics from predictions, certify class-support gates, run
+whole-selection CV, establish a full-agent win, or promote a release. Its
+`promotion` and `ml_quality_promotion_gate_evaluated` fields are always false.
+It does not replay the monotonic admission trace or independently certify an
+early-stop reason; those rely on the frozen core implementation and its
+separate focused tests. Harness fingerprints use repository-relative names
+resolved against the known source root, without machine-specific path literals.
+All original quality/support/CV/full-agent/refit/export/release requirements
+remain in force after this validity gate.
+
+Focused preparation verification passed42 no-fit checks:13 admission,7 original
+HPO,14 anchor/constructor and8 new synthetic-artifact qualification checks.
+The qualifier checks both regression/minimize and classification/maximize.
+Full source/release gates and real paired ML screens have not run for this
+source. The new registry declares472 checks over48 scripts (451 base checks,
+13 admission and8 qualification). Before a future full no-skips source gate,
+provide the ten byte-verified pristine `public_tasks/classification` and
+`public_tasks/regression` inputs; ignored inputs are absent from `git archive`.
+The enclosing common deadline still has to be declared before any execution.
