@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@
+# HPO admission B: predeclared isolated development experiment
+
+Status: prepared on 23 October 2026; no model fit, API call, outer score or
+promotion has been performed for this source. Base is tracked commit
+`bc0603bb17c0680a221d1ba5a9ff3421a9c28ed2`, extracted with `git archive` into
+`work/iteration3-dev`. Canonical source, the active research queue, previous
+archives, measurements and `work/SESSION_STATE.json` are outside this change.
+The companion JSON contains exact controls, hashes, cut order and command
+arguments. A release archive must be made only after review of this source.
+
+## One factor
+
+`optimize_recipe(..., admission='legacy')` retains the default search. Explicit
+`admission='measured'`, runner `--hpo-admission measured`, and development
+benchmark `--admission measured` enable factor B. After the unchanged anchor,
+estimate the next worker cost as `1.5 * median(past successful worker seconds)`.
+Launch the next worker only if the current study budget covers that estimate
+and the existing five-second minimum. A successful observation requires the
+existing finite valid inner objective and a finite positive elapsed duration.
+Measure duration with the coordinator's monotonic clock around the worker
+callback; never trust worker-reported timing for admission. Failed workers
+consume real time but supply no median observation. With no valid positive
+duration, require the full configured worker timeout for subsequent workers.
+Zero, negative and nonfinite durations are excluded and counted.
+
+The anchor is exempt from the median rule. Preserve its existing recipe,
+search-space validation and deadline floor. Check admission before sampling;
+recheck immediately before a unique worker launch so checkpoint/sampler
+overhead cannot spend the admitted allowance. A recheck rejection records the
+sampled recipe as not started and stops; it is not a worker failure or numeric
+objective. Duplicates retain the existing failure handling and are not timing
+observations. Stop at the first refusal; never inspect a future trial's timing
+or score. Keep a successful incumbent even if a later worker is refused. If
+all attempts fail, return the original control and nonnumeric failed values.
+
+No startup or guided-trial reservation is permitted. The prior offline replay
+in `work/hpo_admission_replay.json` found rule A would drop the observed useful
+startup winner; it is rejected. Rule B retained that observed prefix winner,
+but this replay is not a new execution, measured saving, whole-agent identity
+or evidence of TPE superiority. Its clock omitted undistributed nonworker
+overhead. Do not transfer its projected savings into the new benchmark.
+
+Sampler, seed137, startup3, eight trials including anchor, search space, model
+parameters outside the original three searched parameters, features,
+calibration, target/history policy, nested split, objective and worker guards
+remain unchanged. Admission sees elapsed time and success/failure only, never
+objective magnitude or outer labels. The report records the policy, each
+decision, remaining time, estimate, valid history size, post-setup remaining,
+skipped work and reason. Reporting changes do not prove ML improvement.
+
+## Paired screen
+
+Use the strongest historical SINGLE recipes from
+`release/v16-mean1/public-full.json`: regression `/0/selection/0/recipe`
+(as-of history LightGBM with existing `generic_features=missing`) and
+classification `/1/selection/0/recipe` (calibrated
+`feature_views=categorical_te_pair`). They are the benchmark's existing
+portfolio controls. Verify the recipe hashes before fitting. They are not
+the complete V11/V16 ensembles; complete historical scores are not component
+scores. Change neither control features nor its normalization between arms.
+
+Factorial arms are legacy/random, measured/random, legacy/TPE and measured/TPE,
+with an unchanged control refit for comparison. Every inner study gets the
+same 900-second cap, maximum eight trials including anchor, seed137 and
+600-second maximum worker cap. Every worker gets two threads and 1536MiB.
+Use the identical outer cut and saved inner split positions across all four
+arms; any split/hash discrepancy invalidates the pair. Keep failures and
+duplicates in the ledger, without numeric substitutes. Do not prune from
+incomparable intermediate metrics.
+
+Predeclare classification grouped/hash cuts42 and43, and regression forward
+offsets0,1,2. Each study uses only the outer fitting rows and constructs its
+inner holdout there. Refit the selected recipe on that outer fitting
+partition, using the existing further nested stopping/calibration, then
+evaluate the outer holdout. Never use outer scores to continue, admit, sample
+or choose an inner trial. Reuse of public development data remains explicit.
+
+Run one cut per benchmark invocation. Policy order is legacy/measured on
+regression0, measured/legacy on regression1, legacy/measured on regression2,
+legacy/measured on classification42 and measured/legacy on classification43.
+Within each invocation preserve the existing random-then-TPE order. This is
+fixed before outcomes, rather than changed to favour an arm. The companion
+JSON supplies commands with the explicit 900-second study budget. There are
+20 studies across the five cuts. All fits are sequential; freeze sources,
+used tools/tests, task inputs, exact controls and split hashes before starting.
+Use an enclosing owned-process guard and a common coordinator deadline.
+Do not create fresh campaign time for a later arm. If insufficient common
+time remains for a complete pair with full equal study caps and its outer
+refits, leave it pending/partial; a truncated study cannot establish a paired
+win. Admission savings remain unspent, with no reinvestment into more trials,
+seeds, cuts or models in this experiment.
+
+## Outcomes and promotion gates
+
+Report operational outcomes separately: actual elapsed study/worker seconds,
+timeout and other failure counts, complete/startup/guided trials, admitted or
+skipped work and unused allowance. Report outer RMSE for each regression cut
+and Macro F1 for each classification cut, plus per-task means. Do not average
+RMSE and F1 into an invented score or treat failed metrics as zero. An
+operational saving with equal or worse ML quality is not an ML quality gain.
+Equal caps do not imply equal completed work or the same chosen model.
+
+Primary factor comparison is measured versus legacy within each sampler.
+Also compare TPE with random at equal 900-second budgets under the same
+admission policy. A label of TPE with no successful guided trial is not
+evidence of adaptive search. Keep the unchanged SINGLE control in all tables.
+The screen must report every declared cut and all arms, including negative or
+partial results. Do not pool only favourable cuts.
+
+For ML-quality advancement require improved RMSE on every declared forward
+cut or improved Macro F1 on both classification cuts relative to the paired
+legacy arm and unchanged SINGLE control. Report differences against equal
+budget random search; claiming TPE improvement also requires beating its
+mean. In classification, allow no supported class F1 drop greater than0.01
+for classes with at least100 independent fitting feature groups, and report
+gain excluding the rarest class. A timing-only result may be documented as
+operational evidence, without passing this quality gate or changing defaults.
+
+A positive classification screen still needs grouped CV of the entire inner
+selection procedure with exactly-once coverage and separate pooled/fold
+scores. Forward regression is not exactly-once OOF. Before any default or
+release promotion, test the complete candidate agent on both tasks against
+the preserved strongest complete procedure, including refit/export/integrity,
+the full unchanged-source suite plus the new admission tests, and an exact
+unpacked release gate. Source3 remains an unpromoted development prototype.
+Official hidden-test normalized competition points cannot be inferred here.
+
+## Preparation verification
+
+Chronological fake workers with a mocked monotonic clock and real seeded
+Optuna samplers cover fit/unfit budgets, exact boundaries, checkpoint overhead,
+legacy parity, sufficient-budget trace identity, sampler-independent
+admission, successful-winner and all-failed fallbacks, invalid caps and zero
+durations, and poisoning of unused outer labels. No model is fitted by these
+tests. The targeted run passed13 new admission tests,7 original HPO tests and
+14 anchor/constructor tests. The new test is registered in the isolated full
+suite (461 checks over47 scripts); the full suite and release/ML screens
+have not run for this source. Full pass counts must come from later receipts.
